#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281339 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "710d7d7d-97b4-592f-b30c-acf388d38859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v={w}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279617} {:answer/id #uuid "76ca4acf-773c-501c-ba6e-25239ada0435" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279651} {:answer/id #uuid "7b363e77-7f40-535f-a3a7-6bd580690682" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=2w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279692} {:answer/id #uuid "88ce4141-06f6-5738-b4cf-0fb6b9a3a05e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the planes $v=\\pm w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279813} {:answer/id #uuid "eaed37b4-3321-5a47-9faa-28666138fd1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280655}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279813} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcf9576c-0ce8-5723-bb46-cfba69aeb672" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f26bca76-37a5-5f68-8e4a-4d9215b02535" :question/math-academy-id "q-161812" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ {v}^{3}+{w}^{3} \\\\ v+w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u,\\,y(u,v,w)={v}^{3}+{w}^{3},\\,z(u,v,w)=v+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =3{v}^{2} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =3{w}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3{v}^{2} & 3{w}^{2} \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}3{v}^{2} & 3{w}^{2} \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(3{v}^{2}-3{w}^{2}) \\\\  & =3({v}^{2}-{w}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 3({v}^{2}-{w}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ {v}^{2}-{w}^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation ${v}^{2}-{w}^{2}=0$ defines a pair of intersecting planes $v=w$ and $v=-w.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e5c045a-d984-5c99-8fa3-0129ac115c4f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $v={w}^{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278721} {:answer/id #uuid "2d089752-d1ca-57d4-aaad-39bd60fd867f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $vw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278988} {:answer/id #uuid "768c6810-e6a9-5693-b6ba-88bee24c33f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279649} {:answer/id #uuid "9f89b797-8be9-5dae-9e56-f0b7e9d1b9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the sphere ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+{w}^{2}=2.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280008} {:answer/id #uuid "bc5b203f-69ef-5d8b-b9f1-3986949f0305" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $u=w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280247}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279649} :answer-field/id #uuid "55be6ad3-d866-57e2-8467-8385c57eb9ce" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e2d2dfd0-abce-5610-a53e-633420f43575" :question/math-academy-id "q-161815" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{u} \\\\ vw \\\\ u+w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=\\sqrt{u},\\,y(u,v,w)=vw,\\,z(u,v,w)=u+w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =w & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =v \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & w & v \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\begin{vmatrix}w & v \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ w & v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}(w-0)+0 \\\\  & =\\frac{w}{2\\sqrt{u}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{w}{2\\sqrt{u}} & =0 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $w=0$ defines the plane $w=0,$ i.e., $uv$-plane."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281341 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012e5e71-30c4-576f-9027-84673f0cec11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the sphere ${u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+{w}^{2}=3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278593} {:answer/id #uuid "1ca3f8ee-ee06-5aa0-b1ee-b1a91215f89a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=3.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278855} {:answer/id #uuid "aedf9c47-b56b-5e71-845a-05c0a9e74384" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the cylinder ${v}^{2}+{w}^{2}=0.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280139} {:answer/id #uuid "f4e3d435-b0b0-5133-a7de-47ee24110c94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uw-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280736} {:answer/id #uuid "f7242b75-d7a6-5b47-a2a4-a6f542bd4ba3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uv-$plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280754}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278855} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0414cad-2a72-50dc-8e82-0bf67299254f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281140}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5ae1d4bd-a84e-5282-96ec-f8259badfc91" :question/math-academy-id "q-161817" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v{e}^{w} \\\\ 2u+v+3w\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u,\\,y(u,v,w)=v{e}^{w},\\,z(u,v,w)=2u+v+3w.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & ={e}^{w} & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =v{e}^{w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =2 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & {e}^{w} & v{e}^{w} \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}{e}^{w} & v{e}^{w} \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(3{e}^{w}-v{e}^{w}) \\\\  & ={e}^{w}(3-v).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{w}(3-v) & =0 \\\\ 3-v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $3-v=0$ defines the plane $v=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281342 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0360b3bf-0e11-5644-974a-fb91e4539e1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the parabolic cylinder $w=\\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278610} {:answer/id #uuid "40d23535-8e40-5b39-96da-dc0c5913b017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the planes $v=\\pm w.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279167} {:answer/id #uuid "4d4e4c43-7095-567c-8087-ac111d00d4b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=u.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279286} {:answer/id #uuid "a24f7a5b-f9c2-51ab-bfe8-2b6ef54faa12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the $uw-$ plane." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280034} {:answer/id #uuid "c0ca341c-0372-5300-8b3a-24814e46f956" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "The critical points lie on the plane $v=\\frac{3}{4}.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280285}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280285} :answer-field/id #uuid "0966bd13-e522-5f74-88dd-66c421ecae33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5828c68b-3870-5e91-8f73-8351ac68b7ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-161818" :question/problem "Find the locations of all of the critical points of the transformation $T,$ where $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u+3w \\\\ v+2w \\\\ {v}^{2}-u\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "For a transformation \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v \\\\ w\\end{bmatrix}\\to \\begin{bmatrix}x(u,v,w) \\\\ y(u,v,w) \\\\ z(u,v,w)\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nthe Jacobian determinant of $T,$ denoted $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)},$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} & \\frac{∂x}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v} & \\frac{∂y}{∂w} \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & \\frac{∂z}{∂v} & \\frac{∂z}{∂w}\\end{vmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have \n\n$$\nx(u,v,w)=u+3w,\\,y(u,v,w)=v+2w,\\,z(u,v,w)={v}^{2}-u.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂v} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂x}{∂w} & =3 \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & =0 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v} & =1 & \\,\\frac{∂y}{∂w} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{∂z}{∂u} & =-1 & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v} & =2v & \\,\\frac{∂z}{∂w} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the corresponding Jacobian determinant is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix}+3\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =1(0-4v)+3(0+1) \\\\  & =3-4v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe function has critical points when $\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)}=0.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y,z)}{∂(u,v,w)} & =0 \\\\ 3-4v & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation $3-4v=0$ defines the plane $v=\\frac{3}{4}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281348 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23cf8b30-43e0-5d4f-b22f-c7645b490e1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278913} {:answer/id #uuid "b526c5a2-0e99-5af7-b3ee-167c9dc5fbd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280185} {:answer/id #uuid "bcf62e03-74c1-53e9-a7ad-7769e6d2e7e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280253} {:answer/id #uuid "bff9fdb6-2214-5239-bf9b-9a9238bcca31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280280} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ce3585-57f6-59d0-9d8a-aa9eb6b8c4c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280329}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186280185} :answer-field/id #uuid "b15057e1-d960-5add-bef4-5220fa404e1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281145} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30c1db1d-2cc0-5ac8-8f04-c8180becd16a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383542} {:answer/id #uuid "821cd8c6-8ff9-5da6-80d4-645283944e57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383543} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9f678f-6723-5d0a-aaf8-823aac52bf9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383544} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd393ca-0f85-5050-8edc-c100a9d38ea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\,\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383545} {:answer/id #uuid "9ab28153-3505-5ac2-969c-4808d24a5d4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\delta A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383546}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186383545} :answer-field/id #uuid "91eca270-f22e-5746-93f6-648d523d80f9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186383541}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7c1651a7-19c3-5fc6-882f-8612e069dc1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-161831" :question/problem "Consider a small rectangle $Δ$ whose bottom-left corner is located at the point $(-1,1)$ with sides parallel to the coordinate axes in the $uv$-plane and whose area is $\\delta A.$ Which of the following gives the best approximation for the area of the image of this rectangle under the action of the transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}v{e}^{u} \\\\ u{e}^{v}\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the absolute value of the Jacobian determinant gives the local area scale factor of the transformation at that point:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(Δ))≈|\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|\\cdot \\underbrace{\\text{Area}(Δ)}_{\\delta A}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}v{e}^{u} & {e}^{u} \\\\ {e}^{v} & u{e}^{v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =v{e}^{u}\\cdot u{e}^{v}-{e}^{v}\\cdot {e}^{u} \\\\  & =uv{e}^{u+v}-{e}^{u+v} \\\\  & =(uv-1){e}^{u+v} \\\\ {\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}|}_{(-1,1)} & =(uv-1){e}^{u+v}\\,{|}_{u=-1\\,v=1} \\\\  & =(-1\\cdot 1-1){e}^{-1+1} \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(Δ)) & ≈|-2|\\cdot \\delta A \\\\  & =2\\,\\delta A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281352 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48838786-15c4-529e-9b61-9a4ae3631e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/30/3033f0ae73e3f484fc5d3d65e388062feba1824fb3da9971d560cf2f518f49bb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279238} {:answer/id #uuid "644450bf-23df-5be6-9017-bc23e84a13fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/83/8382e54c1f91ff0e07910c1250c046413814748d9e7ef8968984b7223b43afcc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279504} {:answer/id #uuid "71de0d63-b9fe-5bf9-98a3-3aa0f0728bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279627} {:answer/id #uuid "743bb53f-15e9-5c76-9499-48070c482fc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/7f/7f214af0b5d71689ec7f21fff043e1779f1d3244c13fdbaf7b8df7f408d66298.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279641} {:answer/id #uuid "9e8384cd-3f08-52be-b19d-6807ce1004b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/14/1401