030391f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/fe/fe7bb422a3f992ea88a900e63b2c55df99bce3a785929901c248abadfadf23f1.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278998} {:answer/id #uuid "56614d5f-f51d-520c-bd5a-2efe188329bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/30/3033f0ae73e3f484fc5d3d65e388062feba1824fb3da9971d560cf2f518f49bb.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279385} {:answer/id #uuid "63c73c6f-8214-55ad-9f4a-739379cccb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/cb/cb5b22ff46569b231d122c2ed11bd412907f36271a033d86769435adf9fe48c7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279499} {:answer/id #uuid "90ce74d2-cefd-5461-a622-b31141a5968a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279883} {:answer/id #uuid "df833e78-3be8-5410-bdd9-e871a352bba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d4/d477a9f312fc2fb0a5a4c2d13164c96118aa70b53cf23db80be9ec698151e6fd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280563}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186279883} :answer-field/id #uuid "dfbed5de-5d8f-51b2-a9bc-07694301ed70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281224}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "92a30208-5e48-56e6-a327-0e416b1fdedd" :question/math-academy-id "q-161842" :question/problem "Which of the following shows the region in the $uv$-plane where the transformation $T,$ given by \n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} \\\\ u-\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nis (locally) orientation-reversing?" :question/worked-solution "Recall that a transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing at the points where the Jacobian determinant is negative:\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)}<0\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nT:\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}{u}^{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{v}^{2} \\\\ u-\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nComputing the corresponding Jacobian determinant, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂(x,y)}{∂(u,v)} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\frac{∂x}{∂u} & \\frac{∂x}{∂v} \\\\ \\frac{∂y}{∂u} & \\frac{∂y}{∂v}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{vmatrix}3{u}^{2} & -v \\\\ 1 & -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(3{u}^{2})\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)-(1)\\cdot (-v) \\\\  & =v-{u}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the required regions, we solve the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v-{u}^{2} & <0 \\\\ v & <{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNotice that the equation \n\n$$\nv={u}^{2}\n$$\n\ndefines a parabola, and the coordinates of, say, $(1,-1)$ satisfy the inequality. \n\nTherefore, the region where the transformation is (locally) orientation-reversing must be the following:\n\n![](images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281354 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "042e4157-bfc2-5a27-a5f2-30fa623a1739" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c2/c244350524a52123e2e97db4cd8eb4f57737b8b15746eb72a8d54eac32a4f3cf.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278625} {:answer/id #uuid "194e22f8-8fb9-57e0-b1f3-883c6f1f3c27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/c5/c501e7e341af57e86f18d73871314800d453f79572e16ccf2477335352d4dcdc.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278813} {:answer/id #uuid "78185cb7-fed8-5728-84d4-f9c34d0ceb1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/9c/9cd254ac65dedfa4c720b18afd4f5c3c7676b4f21170930f78e9adac276317ee.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279663} {:answer/id #uuid "a94b4a1e-0ac2-5b32-aa1a-639dcba8fbfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/13/1368ee41963c1abcc320d2cd35449c08599582f37c7d68f750e137fcdcd2e57b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186280095} {:answer/id #uuid 